[%# views/entry/form-rte0-warning.tt

A prominent warning shown above the editor when the entry (or restored draft)
was written in the retired rich text editor (rte0) and has been loaded into the
current one. Always rendered so scripts can reveal it for a restored draft; the
hidden field carries the fact through a failed save. (The text itself was already
converted by the server.)

Authors:
    Mark Smith <mark@qq.is>

Copyright (c) 2026 by Dreamwidth Studios, LLC.

This program is free software; you may redistribute it and/or modify it under
the same terms as Perl itself.  For a copy of the license, please reference
'perldoc perlartistic' or 'perldoc perlgpl'.
-%]
[%- form.hidden( name = "rte0_converted", id = "js-rte0-converted", value = rte0_converted ? 1 : 0 ) -%]
<div id="js-rte0-warning" class="alert-box alert rte0-warning[% ' display_none' UNLESS rte0_converted %]" role="alert">[% '.rte0.warning' | ml %]</div>
